      "expected": "Perseverance’s body and other major hardware (such as the\ncruise stage, descent stage, and aeroshell/heat shield) build\nupon the success of NASA’s Curiosity rover and include many\nheritage components. The car-sized Perseverance rover has\nroughly the same dimensions as Curiosity: it’s about 10 feet\nlong (not including the arm), 9 feet wide, and 7 feet tall (about\n3 meters long, 2.7 meters wide, and 2.2 meters tall). But at\n2,260 pounds (1,025 kilograms), Perseverance is about 278\npounds (126 kilograms) heavier than Curiosity."
